---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-presence">
  <Fragment slot="title">9.4 <code>Pres</code> — presence</Fragment>
<p>Presence begins by defining a dynamic field table. Later updates carry
    field handles plus a length-framed data blob whose individual values depend on
    that table.</p>
    <p class="endpoint-index">
      <a href="#presence-field-specs">Pres/1 FieldSpecAnnounce</a><a href="#presence-update">Pres/0 UpdateNotify</a>
      <a href="#presence-statistics-subscribe">Pres/2 StatisticsSubscribe</a><a href="#presence-statistics-update">Pres/3 StatisticsUpdate</a>
      <a href="#presence-temporary">Pres/4 TemporaryPresence</a>
    </p>

    <Endpoint id="presence-field-specs" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/1</code> Presence::FieldSpecAnnounce</Fragment>
      <p>Defines the numeric handles and storage rules used by subsequent presence
      updates.</p>
<pre is:raw><span class="syn-field">definitionCount</span>  <span class="syn-type">u7</span> <span class="syn-comment">0..100 accepted by the current client</span>
<span class="syn-keyword">repeat</span> definitionCount:
    <span class="syn-field">clientOnly</span>   <span class="syn-type">bool</span>
    <span class="syn-field">writable</span>     <span class="syn-type">bool</span>
    <span class="syn-field">ephemeral</span>    <span class="syn-type">bool</span>
    <span class="syn-field">sizeKind</span>     <span class="syn-type">u1</span> <span class="syn-comment">0 = fixed, 1 = variable</span>
    <span class="syn-field">fixedSize?</span>   <span class="syn-type">u16</span>
    <span class="syn-field">serverOnly</span>   <span class="syn-type">bool</span>
    <span class="syn-field">identifier</span>   <span class="syn-type">u8</span>
    <span class="syn-field">handle</span>       <span class="syn-type">u32</span></pre>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-update" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/0</code> Presence::UpdateNotify</Fragment>
      <p>Updates online state and one or more dynamically announced fields. The
      field data is sliced in handle order using each Pres/1 fixed size or the
      next variable size. Cleared handles remove retained values. Local and
      master presence IDs are aliases for the same retained record.</p>
<pre is:raw><span class="syn-keyword">reserved</span>           <span class="syn-type">bits</span>[<span class="syn-number">19</span>]
<span class="syn-field">online</span>             <span class="syn-type">bool</span>
<span class="syn-field">localPresenceId</span>    <span class="syn-type">u32</span>
<span class="syn-field">masterPresenceId</span>   <span class="syn-type">u32</span>
<span class="syn-field">fieldDataByteCount</span> <span class="syn-type">u11</span> <span class="syn-comment">0..1024</span>
<span class="syn-keyword">alignToByte</span>
<span class="syn-field">fieldData</span>          <span class="syn-type">bytes</span>[fieldDataByteCount]
<span class="syn-keyword">reserved</span>           <span class="syn-type">bits</span>[<span class="syn-number">11</span>]
<span class="syn-field">clearedHandles</span>     <span class="syn-type">u32</span>[count:<span class="syn-type">u4</span>]
<span class="syn-field">handles</span>            <span class="syn-type">u32</span>[count:<span class="syn-type">u4</span>]
<span class="syn-field">variableSizes</span>      <span class="syn-type">u16</span>[count:<span class="syn-type">u4</span>]
<span class="syn-field">levelZero?</span>         { <span class="syn-field">isLastPacket</span> <span class="syn-type">bool</span>, <span class="syn-field">target</span> <span class="syn-type">u32</span> }
<span class="syn-field">serverOnly</span>         <span class="syn-type">u8</span></pre>
      <p class="endpoint-note"><code>FIELD_AVATAR</code> (<code>65555</code>) is
      a four-byte <code>ImageTableEntry</code>. Public channel membership usually
      supplies <code>FIELD_TOON_PROFILE</code> (<code>65556</code>) instead; its
      12-byte profile address is followed through <code>Prfl/0</code> path
      <code>04</code> to obtain the selected avatar.</p>
      <p>The client reads more handles than avatar alone. Each slice is the field's
      announced fixed size, or the next variable size, and its bytes are parsed by
      handle id (all multi-byte values big-endian):</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Handle</th><th>Field</th><th>Parse</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>0x50004</code></td><td>clan tag</td><td>byte0 = pair count, byte1 = trailing (0|1); byteCount = pairs&times;2 + trailing; remaining bytes UTF-8</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x00010005</code></td><td>account id</td><td>first four bytes <code>u32</code> (nonzero); the whisper-target account, priority 1</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x0001001b</code></td><td>social account id</td><td>first four bytes <code>u32</code>; account fallback, priority 2</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>65561</code></td><td>toon handle</td><td>region <code>u8</code>, program <code>u32</code>, realm <code>u32</code>, id <code>u64</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>65556</code></td><td>toon profile</td><td>label <code>u32</code>, id <code>u64</code> (a profile address)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>65555</code></td><td>avatar</td><td>tableId <code>u16</code>, offset <code>u16</code> (<code>ImageTableEntry</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x50002</code></td><td>in game</td><td>single byte, true when <code>0x01</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x10020</code> / <code>0x10010</code></td><td>away</td><td>boolean; standing status</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x10022</code> / <code>0x10011</code></td><td>busy</td><td>boolean; standing status</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x00010003</code> / <code>0x00010009</code></td><td>session marks</td><td>set on entry, cleared on exit; presence is held while either is present, and drives leave detection</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="endpoint-note">Standing state resolves with a fixed precedence:
      offline (online = false) wins, then in-game, then the most recently written of
      the busy/away group by write-clock (last write wins), then available. The
      account-id fields are what make an outbound whisper addressable.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-statistics-subscribe" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="live verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/2</code> Presence::StatisticsSubscribe</Fragment>
      <p>Subscribes to, or unsubscribes from, the statistics stream, for parity with
      retail. This is not the mechanism that allocates a whisper-target presence id.</p>
<pre is:raw><span class="syn-field">on</span>  <span class="syn-type">u1</span> <span class="syn-comment">1 = subscribe; whole record is 12 bits (0x420c)</span></pre>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-statistics-update" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="reflected order" status="capture observed">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/3</code> Presence::StatisticsUpdate</Fragment>
      <p>A server statistics update. It carries no hand-written decoder and is read
      entirely from the embedded metadata type. It is a legitimate record: leaving
      it unmapped closed the session on the first statistics update.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-temporary" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/4</code> Presence::TemporaryPresence</Fragment>
      <p>Asks the server to allocate a connection-local presence id for one or more
      target toons &mdash; the step that makes a stranger whisperable. The allocated
      id is delivered asynchronously in a later <code>Pres/0</code> update, not in
      the response.</p>
<pre is:raw><span class="syn-field">toonList</span>  <span class="syn-type">array</span>&lt;<span class="syn-type">ToonHandle</span>&gt; <span class="syn-comment">1..10</span>
<span class="syn-type">ToonHandle</span> { <span class="syn-field">region</span> <span class="syn-type">integer</span>, <span class="syn-field">programId</span> <span class="syn-type">FourCC</span>, <span class="syn-field">realm</span> <span class="syn-type">integer</span>, <span class="syn-field">id</span> <span class="syn-type">u64</span> }</pre>
      <p class="endpoint-note">The program id must be a FourCC, not a generic
      integer.</p>
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
